    "maintainer_can_modify": true,
    "title": "examples: exit with failure if signature verification fails",
    "user": {
      "login": "amartya1523",
      "id": 133855728,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOB_p58A",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/133855728?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/amartya1523",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/amartya1523",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amartya1523/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amartya1523/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amartya1523/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amartya1523/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amartya1523/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amartya1523/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amartya1523/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amartya1523/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amartya1523/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "The ecdsa and schnorr examples print whether the signature verified, but return `EXIT_SUCCESS` either way. Both build systems run the examples as tests, so if verification broke, those test runs would still pass.\n\nI checked this by flipping a byte of the signature (schnorr) and of the message hash (ecdsa) right before verification: both examples printed \"Is the signature valid? false\" and `ctest -R \"example\\.(schnorr|ecdsa)\"` still reported them as passed. With this change the same experiment makes both tests fail.\n\nThis matches what the musig example already does when `secp256k1_schnorrsig_verify` fails. The return stays at the end of `main`, so the context destroy and secret key erasure still happen first.",
    "labels": [],
